---
description: Save a durable, verified fact or preference in the local Markdown memory vault
argument-hint: "<fact, preference, decision, or lesson>"
---
Record the following information in the private Markdown memory vault under
`~/.pi/memory/`:

$ARGUMENTS

Load the `persistent-memory` skill and read the relevant vault indexes and
existing notes first. If no information was provided, ask what should be
remembered. Save only a durable, confirmed, non-sensitive fact; choose the
narrowest appropriate user, project, or topic scope; and update an existing
note instead of adding a duplicate. Before the first write, verify that the
vault is its own Jujutsu repository and create a new, specifically described
`[π]` revision. Maintain any necessary index links and snapshot the completed
changes with `jj -R "$HOME/.pi/memory" status`.

If the information is ambiguous, sensitive, unverified, or too ephemeral to
retain, explain why and ask for clarification rather than storing it. Finish by
stating exactly what was saved and which note was changed.
